【中文】

1. 定义

   1.1 「本软件」：Aora Bot 仓库主分支及 @aora-bot/* npm 包中的全部内容，
       包括源代码、角色设计（角色造型、配色、五官、动画状态及其数据）、
       文档、图片与示例。
       仓库 emotion-ball 分支中的 Emotion Ball 表情馆经典版不适用本协议，
       以该分支内的许可文件为准。

   1.2 「你」：使用本软件的个人或组织。组织的人数，与控制它、受它控制
       或与它受同一方控制的关联组织合并计算。

   1.3 「免费使用者」：符合以下任一条件的你——
       (a) 以个人身份使用的个人，包括独立开发者为自己的产品使用；
       (b) 学生、教师与教育机构，用于教学、学习与研究；
       (c) 非营利组织；
       (d) 以开源许可公开全部源代码、且不以营利为目的的开源项目；
       (e) 全职、兼职及长期外包人员合计不超过 3 人的营利组织。

   1.4 为他人开发产品时（例如外包或受雇开发），以最终拥有或运营该
       产品的一方判断是否属于免费使用者。

2. 免费使用者的授权

   在遵守本协议的前提下，免费使用者可以免费、非独占、在全球范围内
   使用、复制、修改本软件，将其集成到自己的网站、应用、游戏、硬件
   设备及其他产品或服务中（包括商业用途），并随该产品或服务分发。

3. 其他组织

   3.1 不属于免费使用者的组织，在已上线的产品、服务或任何商业用途中
       使用本软件，须事先取得商业授权。通用条款见仓库根目录的
       LICENSE-COMMERCIAL.md：
       https://github.com/sam70361/aora-bot/blob/main/LICENSE-COMMERCIAL.md

   3.2 在取得商业授权之前，这类组织可以免费将本软件用于评估、内部测试
       与原型开发，但不得用于已上线的产品或服务。

4. 所有人都不得从事的行为

   以下行为适用于所有人，包括已取得商业授权的被许可方，除非与著作权人
   另行书面约定：

   (a) 将本软件或其修改版本作为主体单独出售、出租或付费分发，例如以
       组件库、模板、UI 套件、源码包、SDK 或插件的形式；
   (b) 提供以本软件为主要价值的托管服务或接口，例如角色生成、头像生成
       或表情动画服务；
   (c) 将角色形象单独制成商品出售，包括贴纸、表情包、周边、印刷品与
       数字藏品，或单独出售导出的图片、动画与素材包；
   (d) 将角色名称或形象申请注册为商标，或声称拥有其著作权；
   (e) 使用本软件的角色设计训练或微调用于生成角色形象的 AI 模型；
   (f) 删除或修改本软件中的版权与许可声明。

   在自己的产品中把角色用作头像、助手形象或吉祥物，不属于上述行为。

5. 声明与署名

   5.1 分发本软件或其修改版本的源代码时，须完整保留本协议与版权声明。

   5.2 免费使用者公开发布、上线或分发使用了本软件的产品或服务时，
       须在以下任一位置注明本软件的出处：
       (a) 产品的「关于」「致谢」「帮助」或设置页面；
       (b) 网站页脚；
       (c) 应用商店、插件市场或项目主页上的产品说明；
       (d) 产品的 README、文档或第三方许可清单；
       (e) 无法放置链接的产品（例如硬件设备、离线软件或游戏）的说明书、
           包装、片尾字幕或制作人员名单，并以文字写明完整网址。
       署名须包含「Aora Bot」字样，并链接至本软件的代码仓库
       https://github.com/sam70361/aora-bot 或著作权人日后公布的官方
       网站，例如「Powered by Aora Bot」或「角色由 Aora Bot 提供」。
       署名无须紧邻角色展示，但不得暗示著作权人为该产品提供背书。

   5.3 个人自用、学习研究、内部测试及尚未公开发布的使用，无须署名。

   5.4 已取得商业授权的被许可方，可依商业授权条款免于署名。

6. 修改与贡献

   6.1 你对本软件所做的修改由你享有，但修改后的版本仍受本协议约束。

   6.2 你向本仓库提交的贡献（例如 Pull Request），即视为你同意著作权人
       可以按本协议及商业授权条款使用、修改与分发该贡献。

7. 终止

   违反本协议的，本协议授予你的权利自动终止。你在收到著作权人书面
   （含邮件）通知后 30 日内纠正违约行为的，授权恢复；再次违约的，
   不再恢复。

8. 无担保与责任限制

   本软件按「现状」提供，不附带任何明示或默示的担保，包括但不限于
   适销性、特定用途适用性及不侵权担保。在适用法律允许的最大范围内，
   著作权人不对因使用本软件产生的任何损失承担责任。

9. 法律适用与争议解决

   本协议适用中华人民共和国法律。因本协议产生的争议，双方应友好协商
   解决；协商不成的，任何一方可向著作权人所在地有管辖权的人民法院
   提起诉讼。

[English]

1. Definitions

   1.1 "The Software" means everything in the main branch of the Aora Bot
       repository and in the @aora-bot/* npm packages, including the source
       code, the character designs (shapes, colours, faces, animation states
       and their data), documentation, images and examples. The classic
       Emotion Ball edition in the repository's emotion-ball branch is not
       covered by this license and is governed by the license files in that
       branch.

   1.2 "You" means the individual or organisation using the Software. An
       organisation's headcount includes every organisation that controls
       it, is controlled by it, or is under common control with it.

   1.3 "Free User" means you, if any of the following applies:
       (a) you are an individual using the Software in your own name,
           including an independent developer using it in your own products;
       (b) you are a student, teacher or educational institution using it
           for teaching, learning or research;
       (c) you are a non-profit organisation;
       (d) you are an open-source project that publishes all of its source
           code under an open-source license and does not operate for
           profit;
       (e) you are a for-profit organisation with no more than 3 people in
           total, counting full-time, part-time and long-term contracted
           staff.

   1.4 When you build a product for someone else (for example as a
       contractor or employee), whether the use is free is decided by the
       party that ultimately owns or operates that product.

2. Grant to Free Users

   Subject to this license, Free Users may use, copy and modify the
   Software free of charge, on a non-exclusive and worldwide basis,
   integrate it into their own websites, apps, games, hardware devices and
   other products or services (including for commercial purposes), and
   distribute it as part of those products or services.

3. Other organisations

   3.1 An organisation that is not a Free User needs a commercial license
       before using the Software in a live product or service, or for any
       other commercial purpose. The general terms are in
       LICENSE-COMMERCIAL.md at the repository root:
       https://github.com/sam70361/aora-bot/blob/main/LICENSE-COMMERCIAL.md

   3.2 Until it obtains a commercial license, such an organisation may use
       the Software free of charge for evaluation, internal testing and
       prototyping, but not in a live product or service.

4. Restrictions for everyone

   The following apply to everyone, including commercial licensees, unless
   otherwise agreed in writing with the copyright holder. You may not:

   (a) sell, rent or distribute for a fee the Software or a modified version
       of it as a product in its own right, for example as a component
       library, template, UI kit, source bundle, SDK or plugin;
   (b) offer a hosted service or API whose main value is the Software, for
       example a character, avatar or animated-expression service;
   (c) sell the characters as goods in their own right, including stickers,
       sticker packs, merchandise, prints and digital collectibles, or sell
       exported images, animations or asset packs on their own;
   (d) register a character's name or appearance as a trademark, or claim
       copyright in it;
   (e) use the Software's character designs to train or fine-tune AI models
       that generate character designs;
   (f) remove or alter the copyright and license notices in the Software.

   Using a character as an avatar, assistant or mascot in your own product
   is not one of the above.

5. Notices and attribution

   5.1 When you distribute the source code of the Software or of a modified
       version, you must keep this license and the copyright notice intact.

   5.2 When a Free User publicly releases, launches or distributes a product
       or service that uses the Software, it must credit the Software in any
       one of these places:
       (a) the product's About, Credits, Help or settings page;
       (b) the website footer;
       (c) the product description in an app store, a plugin marketplace or
           on the project's homepage;
       (d) the product's README, documentation or third-party license list;
       (e) for a product that cannot carry a link, such as a hardware device,
           offline software or a game: its manual, packaging, end credits or
           staff list, with the full URL written out.
       The credit must include the words "Aora Bot" and link to the
       Software's repository at https://github.com/sam70361/aora-bot or to an
       official website the copyright holder announces later, for example
       "Powered by Aora Bot". It need not appear next to the characters, but
       it must not suggest that the copyright holder endorses the product.

   5.3 No credit is required for personal use, learning and research,
       internal testing, or anything not yet publicly released.

   5.4 A commercial licensee may omit the credit under the terms of its
       commercial license.

6. Modifications and contributions

   6.1 You own the modifications you make, but the modified version remains
       subject to this license.

   6.2 By submitting a contribution to this repository (for example a pull
       request), you agree that the copyright holder may use, modify and
       distribute it under this license and under commercial license terms.

7. Termination

   If you breach this license, the rights it grants you end automatically.
   If you cure the breach within 30 days of written notice (including email)
   from the copyright holder, your rights are reinstated; they are not
   reinstated after a second breach.

8. No warranty and limitation of liability

   The Software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express
   or implied, including merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose
   and non-infringement. To the fullest extent permitted by law, the
   copyright holder is not liable for any loss arising from use of the
   Software.

9. Governing law and disputes

   This license is governed by the laws of the People's Republic of China.
   Disputes shall first be settled through friendly negotiation; failing
   that, either party may bring the dispute before the competent people's
   court where the copyright holder is located.
